From: somestupidgirl <sunnevanattsol@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] copyfile: xattr_flags.c without the private XPC header

xattr_flags.c includes <xpc/private.h> for one call,
_xpc_runtime_is_app_sandboxed(), which picks the sandboxed or unboxed
default property table.  libxpc exports it and the SDK's libxpc stub
lists it, but Apple publish no header for it.  Disassembled from libxpc
in macOS 26.5.2's dyld shared cache, it reads no argument and returns a
byte loaded into w0 -- bool (void).  Include the private header where it
exists and declare that otherwise.

--- a/xattr_flags.c	2026-09-15 05:01:33
+++ b/xattr_flags.c	2026-09-15 05:01:33
@@ -33,7 +33,14 @@
 #include <sys/types.h>
 #include <sys/xattr.h>
 #include <dispatch/dispatch.h>
+#if __has_include(<xpc/private.h>)
 #include <xpc/private.h>
+#else
+#include <stdbool.h>
+/* libxpc's exported SPI; no published header declares it.  Takes nothing
+ * and returns a byte, read from libxpc in macOS 26.5.2's shared cache. */
+bool _xpc_runtime_is_app_sandboxed(void);
+#endif
 
 #define FLAG_DELIM_CHAR	'#'
 #define FLAG_DELIM_STR "#"
